{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966798,"nonce":"ScsyAtLnhUN/6Gl/ntcGpQWlW+Q=","title":"P4.3 motion-subtree bake initially broke widgets inside ancestor overflow clips","message":"Three widgets regressed simultaneously when P4.3 wired the walker gate\n(`pushed_for_motion_subtree`) on 2026-05-26:\n\n- **`cn::progress_animated`** — clicking Replay does nothing; blue bar\n  reappears only when the user hovers a sibling button.\n- **`cn::switch`** — thumb visually displaced relative to its track;\n  toggling Notifications visually corrupts; Dark mode's whole switch\n  appears moved.\n- **`cn::spinner`** — blue arc gone entirely.\n\nThe hover-then-appears symptom is the giveaway: the slow-path repaint\nfired by `:hover` bypasses the bake and re-walks the subtree directly,\nso the widget paints correctly for that one frame. As soon as a fast-\npath frame returns, the broken bake re-applies.\n\n\nBlinc stores clip rects **per-primitive in screen coordinates** (a\n`clip_rect` field on `GpuPrimitive`, applied in the SDF shader). The\nP4.3 model assumed `push_composite_layer` peels emission into a clean\nscratch batch that bakes the subtree as if drawing onto a fresh\ntexture — but it does NOT reset / strip the clip stack. Every primitive\nemitted into the scratch batch carries the active screen-space clip.\n\nFor `cn::progress_animated` specifically, the indicator is positioned\nat `left(-width)` inside a `.overflow_clip()` track. At base state\n(`translate_x = 0`) the indicator is fully outside the track's clip\nrect — every primitive's `clip_rect` rejects it in the shader → the\nbaked texture is fully transparent. The per-frame motion overlay\n(`composite_motion_layers_overlay`) then blits that empty texture at\n`screen_aabb + translate_x*dpi`. No matter how large `translate_x`\ngets, the texture has no visible pixels to show, so the bar is\ninvisible until a non-baked repaint fires.\n\n`cn::switch` and `cn::spinner` hit similar but less catastrophic\nvariants — the thumb / arc lives inside a clipped pill / rotated\nviewport, so the bake captures the wrong slice and the blit applies\nthe wrong dest_pos.\n\n\n`push_composite_layer` in [paint.rs](crates/blinc_gpu/src/paint.rs)\nnow snapshots `composite_layer_clip_base = clip_stack.len()`. While\nemission is routed to a scratch batch, `get_clip_data` reads\n`clip_stack[clip_base..]` only — so ancestor clips below the snapshot\nare excluded from per-primitive `clip_rect` (the subtree's own\nintrinsic clips still apply normally).\n\nThe walker captures `ctx.current_clip_aabb()` BEFORE the push and\nthreads it through `DynamicKind::{MotionSubtreeTexture,CssAnimated}.ambient_clip`.\nBoth overlays (`composite_motion_layers_overlay`,\n`composite_css_layers_overlay`) pass that AABB as the `clip` arg to\n`blit_tight_texture_to_target`, which uses it as the blit scissor.\nResult: the texture can translate/scale freely; only the SCISSOR\ndefines what's visible at composite time, and the scissor is the\nancestor clip — so the animation sweeps ACROSS the clip rather than\ndragging a baked-in clipped slice with it.\n\nVerification:\n- New tests `composite_layer_strips_ancestor_clip_from_emit` +\n  `composite_layer_preserves_inner_clip` in `paint.rs` (passing).\n- Workspace: 808 tests pass post-fix.\n\n\n**Walker gate WAS hard-disabled** earlier in this commit chain in\n[`renderer/paint/motion.rs:585`](crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/paint/motion.rs#L585) —\n`pushed_for_motion_subtree = false` regardless of candidate set. All\nother P4.3 scaffolding stays in place so the proper fix can land\nincrementally:\n\n- `DynamicKind::MotionSubtreeTexture` variant (currently unused but\n  exhaustive matches stay correct)\n- `subtree_texture_candidates` set (P4.1 detection — still computed\n  per frame; cheap)\n- `MotionSubtreeBakeRegistry` + `prepare` / `mark_baked` /\n  `invalidate` / `demote_lapsed` (tests still pass, real paths never\n  call them when the gate is off)\n- `WindowedContext::motion_subtree_textures` map + bake hook + blit\n  overlay (all skip silently when no `MotionSubtreeTexture` regions\n  exist)\n\n\n\nReject any subtree whose root has an active `overflow_clip` between it\nand the surface. The walker can query `ctx.current_clip_aabb()` at the\ngate site and bail when the clip is tighter than the subtree's natural\nbounds. Conservative but ships fast. Loses bake-path perf for\n`progress_animated` (the most common motion-bound widget) — only\n`cn::toast` slide-in and `cn::drawer` enter would qualify.\n\n\nWhen `push_composite_layer` redirects emission, ALSO reset the clip\nstack in the scratch batch's primitive emit path — i.e. clear\n`clip_rect` on every primitive going into scratch — and propagate the\ncaptured ambient clip to the per-frame blit instead. The blit calls\n[`blit_tight_texture_to_target`](crates/blinc_gpu/src/renderer.rs) and\nalready accepts an optional clip rect via the final two `None`\npositional args — extend that path so each `MotionCompositeJob` carries\nits `ambient.clip_aabb` and passes it through.\n\nThis recovers the bake path for clipped subtrees but requires:\n1. New `push_composite_layer_strip_clips()` mode in `GpuPaintContext`\n2. `composite_motion_layers_overlay` to pass the ambient clip into the\n   blit\n3. Test coverage in `motion_texture_cache.rs` for the strip-clips\n   behaviour\n\n\nAdd a `rotate_z` path AND a `scissor_rect` uniform to the blit shader.\nSolves rotation (currently elided in both CSS + motion overlays) and\nclipping in one shot. Largest scope but cleanest end state.\n\n\n- `progress_animated_bakes_unclipped_indicator` — `prepare` +\n  `mark_baked` flow on a subtree inside an `.overflow_clip()`, assert\n  the baked texture has non-transparent pixels at the indicator's\n  drawn region.\n- `spinner_rotation_blit_applies_live_angle` — once Option B/C lands,\n  verify the blit transform tracks `MotionBindings::get_rotation()`.\n- `cn_switch_thumb_blit_dest_pos` — assert blit `dest_pos.x` tracks\n  `translate_x` without ambient clip interference.\n\n\n```rust\nuse blinc_cn::prelude::*;\nlet value = ctx.use_animated_value_for(\"v\", 0.0, ...);\ndiv().child(cn::progress_animated(value).w(250.0))\n```\n\nClick any button that bumps `value.set_target(250.0)` — bar should\nsmoothly fill. With the gate enabled it stays invisible until any\nsibling hover fires. With the gate disabled (current state) it works.","files":null}]}